# Introduction to Inner class in java
-- Inner class :- An inner class in java is a class that is defined within another class.
-- inner class helps logically group related functionality makin g the code more modular to earlier to manage

** 4types of inner class:-
1. member inner clas:- define inside another class typically creating object closely related to the outern class.
2. static inner class:- define inside a class but donot need an instance of the outer class
3. Local inner class:- Define within methods useful for temporary tasks
4. anonymus class:- class without names, creation on -the - fly for short term use.

1. member inner class
package com.kod.memberInnerclass;

public class Program1 {
	int a  = 10;
	class Program2
	{
		int b = 20;
		void dispProgram2()
		{
			System.out.println(a);
			System.out.println(b);
		}
	}
	void dispProgram1()
	{
		System.out.println(a);
		Program2 p2 = new Program2();
		p2.dispProgram2();
	}
}

// main  class

public class Main {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Program1 p1 = new Program1();   // create outer class object
		p1.dispProgram1();
		//Program2 p2 = new Program2();  // Error
		// can't go out of the class it is not possible to create object of which class --> member inner class
		// 
		
		// alternative way of member innerclass
		Program1.Program2 p2 = p1.new Program2();
		p2.dispProgram2();;
	}
}



2. static nested class:-
public class Program1 {
	int a  = 10;
static	class Program2
	{
		static int b = 20;
	static	void dispProgram2()
		{
			System.out.println(b);
		}
	}
	void dispProgram1()
	{
		System.out.println(a);
		Program2 p2 = new Program2();
		p2.dispProgram2();
	}
}

// main  class

public class Main {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
Program1.Program2.dispProgram2();
	}
}

